    "collapsible_content_jF6Q7J": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_UHMcUe": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "My Phoenix Gravity Water Filter has water dripping between the Upper and Lower Chambers. What does this mean?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>This will be from over-filling the Water Filter System. Careful use can help prevent overfilling by checking how much water is in the lower chamber before filling the upper chamber. Once you get to know your usage rates the re-filling process will become second nature! We also sell a vision tap which will enable you to see the water level from the outside.<a href=\"/products/vision-tap-stainless-steel\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Vision Tap- Stainless Steel\"> </a>Please visit our <a href=\"/products/vision-tap-stainless-steel\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Vision Tap- Stainless Steel\">Vision Tap page</a> for more information .</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_D7di3E": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What certifications do Phoenix Gravity Water Filters have, and which products do they apply to?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Phoenix Gravity Water Filters are independently certified to NSF/ANSI 42, 372, and 401 standards, covering contaminant reduction, material safety, and emerging contaminants such as PFAS and microplastics. These certifications apply to the Phoenix Gravity Water Filter systems and relevant filtration components.</p><p>Carbon Cartridges - NSF/ANSI 42 (safely reduces non-health-related contaminants that impact the taste, odor, or visual appearance of water such as chlorine, particulates and iron) </p><p>Filter System - NSF/ANSI 42 (safely reduces non-health-related contaminants that impact the taste, odor, or visual appearance of water such as chlorine, particulates and iron) & NSF/ANSI/CAN 372 (standard that establishes testing methods and verification procedures for the \"lead-free\" content of drinking water system components) </p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_H8Qyp3": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why is my water cloudy?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Don’t worry, cloudy water after initial installation is normal and completely harmless. It’s simply safe residual dust from the manufacturing process. It can occur if the cartridges are not correctly primed - and we recommend priming cartridges fully (see above). If it is not primed, it can take about four rounds of filtered water to clear.   <br/>please refer to our instruction manual sheet <a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0735/1821/9557/files/Phoenix_Gravity___Carbon_Filter.pdf\">instruction manual sheet .</a></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_H6C73A": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Does Phoenix Gravity water filters remove limescale ?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p><br/>Our filters do not remove limescale, as it is primarily made up of calcium and magnesium, which are essential minerals that your body needs.</p><p>Our system is specifically designed to remove harmful contaminants while retaining beneficial minerals like these. As a result, a small amount of limescale is completely normal and does not affect the quality or safety of your filtered water. (possibly mention TDS?)</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_W4xnAC": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I clean my filter?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p><strong>Gravity Filter:</strong>We recommend hand washing using warm soapy water and a non-abrasive cloth or sponge. Then, leave to air dry or buff with a microfiber cloth. (Don’t forget to remove your cartridges first!)</p><p><strong>Cartridges:</strong>Wash these under cold running water only and using a mildly abrasive scourer or brush, gently massage along cartridges from mount to end only - to avoid contamination.</p><p><strong>POSTreat:</strong>Again, use warm soapy water and a non-abrasive cloth/ sponge. Then, leave to air dry or buff with a microfiber cloth. (Don’t forget to remove the media first!)</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_tWhmT6": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I set it up myself?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Certainly! Our systems are designed to be extremely easy to assemble and everything you need will be included. You can do it yourself with just your hands - there’s no specialist tools, plumbers or electricians required.We include full instructions with every unit and we’re always here to help. You can contact us <a href=\"/pages/get-help\" title=\"New Get Help\">here.</a></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
